  301                 /               TOTALLY COMPATIBLE WITH RX01 OPERATIONS EXCEPT FOR THE ANOMALOUS\par
  302                 /               "RX02" BIT[8] WHICH INDICATES THE DRIVE IS AN RX02 ONLY ON AN RX02!\par
  303                 /               IT MEANS WRITE-PROTECT ON AN RX01 OR DSD-210. SINCE THIS BIT IS\par
  304                 /               THEREFORE WORTHLESS, THIS SEEMS UNIMPORTANT. HOWEVER, MANY EXISTING\par
  305                 /               SOFTWARE PACKAGES HANDLE THIS SITUATION WRONG AND BELIEVE BIT[8] TO\par
  306                 /               ALWAYS INDICATE RX02 VALIDITY. THIS HANDLER WILL NOT "SCREW UP" ON\par
  307                 /               THIS BIT, ALWAYS CHECKING THE DRIVE TYPE BY THE "READ-STATUS\par
  308                 /               DOUBLE-DENSITY" METHOD.\par
